{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ובקצרכם", :translit "uv'kutzrachem", :gloss "and when you reap"} {:he "ובקציר כם", :translit "uv'katzir cham", :gloss "and in harvest of them"} {:he "סמ\"ך", :translit "samach", :gloss "support"} {:he "קציר", :translit "katzir", :gloss "harvest"} {:he "קצרוהו לסטים", :translit "katzruhu listim", :gloss "bandits harvested it"} {:he "כרסמוהו נמלים", :translit "charsumohu nemalim", :gloss "ants gnawed it"} {:he "שברתו הרוח", :translit "shabarto ha-ruach", :gloss "the wind broke it"} {:he "אכלתו בהמה", :translit "achalto behemah", :gloss "an animal ate it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["קציר" "קציר" "קציר" "קציר"]} {:kind :other, :note "Qere reading ובקצירכם reshapes the ketiv to demand leaving pe'ah; four occurrences of קציר exclude four cases of pre-damage from obligation."}], :frame {:text "Mishnah Pe'ah 4:1 lists cases where grain already affected before the farmer completed the harvest does not count toward the pe'ah obligation: if bandits cut it (קצרוהו לסטים), if wind broke it, if ants gnawed it, or if an animal ate it. Each removes the grain from the category of 'your harvest' that the verse commands to leave for the poor.", :sources ["Mishnah Pe'ah 4:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "פאת שדך", :translit "pe'at sadecha", :gloss "corner of your field"} {:he "הפיאה", :translit "ha-pe'ah", :gloss "the pe'ah"} {:he "אחד מששים", :translit "echad mishishim", :gloss "one from sixty"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "פאת שדך", :b "אחד מששים"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'one part in sixty' is recorded as a measure for pe'ah. Tosefta Pe'ah 3:7 cites Beit Shammai as setting the measure of pe'ah at one part in sixty, while the Mishnah Pe'ah 1:2 states explicitly that there is no fixed measure, allowing any amount.", :sources ["Mishnah Pe'ah 1:2" "Tosefta Pe'ah 3:7"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ונכרתה", :translit "venichr'tah", :gloss "and shall be cut off"} {:he "ובקצרכם", :translit "uv'kutzrachem", :gloss "and when you reap"} {:he "נפש", :translit "nefesh", :gloss "a soul"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah: verse 20's ונכרתה is read alongside verse 9's ובקצרכם; the word נפש at the end of verse 8 links karet to robbing the poor."}], :frame {:text "Leviticus 19:8 states that one who eats a shelamim offering on the third day bears his iniquity and that soul (הנפש ההיא) shall be cut off (ונכרתה) from his people. Leviticus 19:9–10 immediately follows with the commandments of pe'ah, leket, and peret given to the poor. Leviticus 19:8 uses the word נפש in the phrase הנפש ההיא ונכרתה, and the rabbis interpret the karet punishment as extending to one who withholds the poor-due.", :sources ["Leviticus 19:8" "Leviticus 19:9–10"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["קציר" "קציר" "קציר" "קציר"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "קציר", :refs ["Genesis 30:14" "Exodus 34:22" "Leviticus 19:9" "Leviticus 23:22" "Joshua 3:15" "Judges 15:1" "1 Samuel 6:13" "1 Samuel 12:17"], :n 26, :lens :exact} {:phrase "קציר", :refs ["Genesis 30:14" "Exodus 34:22" "Leviticus 19:9" "Leviticus 23:22" "Joshua 3:15" "Judges 15:1" "1 Samuel 6:13" "1 Samuel 12:17"], :n 26, :lens :exact} {:phrase "קציר", :refs ["Genesis 30:14" "Exodus 34:22" "Leviticus 19:9" "Leviticus 23:22" "Joshua 3:15" "Judges 15:1" "1 Samuel 6:13" "1 Samuel 12:17"], :n 26, :lens :exact} {:phrase "קציר", :refs ["Genesis 30:14" "Exodus 34:22" "Leviticus 19:9" "Leviticus 23:22" "Joshua 3:15" "Judges 15:1" "1 Samuel 6:13" "1 Samuel 12:17"], :n 26, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Qere reading ובקצירכם reshapes the ketiv to demand leaving pe'ah; four occurrences of קציר exclude four cases of pre-damage from obligation.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "פאת שדך", :a-value 805, :b "אחד מששים", :b-value 703, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Semikhah: verse 20's ונכרתה is read alongside verse 9's ובקצרכם; the word נפש at the end of verse 8 links karet to robbing the poor.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:24:21.156167723Z", :model "glm-5.2"}